<title>FRANCE: CGT urges French defence workers to step up fight.</title>
<headline>CGT urges French defence workers to step up fight.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Communist-led CGT union urged French state workers on Thursday to step up efforts to fight government restructuring plans in the defence sector during labour actions planned between December 9 and December 20.</p>
<p>It said the government's decision on Wednesday to backtrack on plans to privatise electronics group Thomson by selling it to Lagardere had put &quot;new wind in the fight.&quot;</p>
<p>The union is demanding that a young worker be hired to compensate for each departing worker in the sector and pushing to retain special pension arrangements.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452 (c) Reuters Limited 1996</p>
